# Out of the Hollow Mouth at dawn, then the walk up the south trail to Highbank (scripts/mouth_escape.gd).
# Claude's draft lines for Preston, 2026-10-11 (Preston: the partner should explain the courier side, that it
# wants into the Wayline and needs a partner, so the theft at the Job Board makes sense). Proposals, edit freely.
# Same rules as flood_bank.dialogue: "Name: line" is spoken, a bare line is narration, [#face] picks the
# portrait, "- " lines are choices. "do walk_on()" moves the two of you a stretch further up the trail.
# How we write: docs/design/dialogue-voice-guide.md.
# Claude, 2026-10-26 (placeholder factory lane S): split into beats. "start" plays on the dawn bank
# (scripts/mouth_escape.gd); each title after it plays on the road up to Highbank (scripts/story/route_scene.gd,
# scenes/road_to_highbank.tscn) when the party reaches its spot on the trail, and the party strolls on while a line is
# up, so the old "do walk_on()" steps are gone. Every line from before is kept word for word and in order. Lines
# under a "NEW, proposal" comment are Claude's proposals in the St. Joseph voice, for Preston to keep, change or cut:
# the lost parcel in the mud and the view from the rise.

~ start
You come up out of the dark into gray morning light. The rain has quit.
{{partner_name}}: [#surprised] ...Huh. Would you look at that. The sun actually came up.
{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] We made it! We actually made it out of there!
Behind you the ruin sits high and dry on its stones, like it's been there forever.
The river has gone down to a sulk.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] That thing was not there yesterday. I've walked this bank my whole life.
- What was that place?
	{{partner_name}}: [#worried] A Hollow. Folks call 'em that, the holes that open up in the river.
	{{partner_name}}: [#worried] Nobody's real sure where they come from.
	{{partner_name}}: [#worried] Things live down there. Things that don't much care for company. You saw.
- Is the parcel okay?
	{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] Dry as a bone. Don't ask me how, but I'm not complaining.
{{partner_name}}: [#determined] C'mon. Highbank's up the south trail. Walk with me, I'll fill you in on the way.
=> END

~ trail_bluff
# By the washed-out ferry sign.
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] So. Highbank sits way up on the bluff, so the water never gets it.
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] Every town on this river leans on it.
{{partner_name}}: Down here the roads wash out every spring.
{{partner_name}}: Only way anything gets anywhere is if somebody carries it.
{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] That's the Wayline. Couriers. Runners, we call 'em.
{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] Mail, medicine, seed, whatever needs going, a runner takes it. Through a Hollow if they have to.
=> END

~ trail_tower
# At the Wayline waymark post.
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] The Wayline Tower's right in the middle of town. Starward runs it. The Postmaster.
- You want to be a runner.
	{{partner_name}}: [#sad] ...Is it that obvious? Yeah. Since I was little.
- So you're a runner?
	{{partner_name}}: [#sad] Not yet. Trainee. Been one a good while, too.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] Starward's got one rule that won't budge. Nobody runs a route alone.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] You run with a partner or you don't run.
{{partner_name}}: [#sad] And every runner's already paired up.
{{partner_name}}: [#sad] Nobody wants the trainee who's never carried a thing.
=> END

~ trail_parcel
# NEW, proposal (Claude, 2026-10-26): a lost parcel half sunk in the mud. The lines from before follow it.
A parcel sits half sunk in the mud at the edge of the trail, its twine gone black with river water.
{{partner_name}}: [#sad] Aw, no. Look at that.
{{partner_name}}: [#sad] Somebody's letter, I bet. Floated down from who knows where.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] No mark on it I can read. Whoever's waiting on that one is still waiting.
# From before.
{{partner_name}}: [#determined] But this right here is Wayline mail I pulled out of a flood.
{{partner_name}}: [#determined] If I walk it through that door myself, they gotta take me serious.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] ...Only I'd need a partner standing next to me when I do it.
{{partner_name}} goes quiet for a few steps.
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] I mean. You did follow me through a whole Hollow without running off.
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] That's more than most.
- I'll be your partner.
	{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] For real? You're not just saying that? ...Okay. Okay! Partners!
- Let's see how it goes.
	{{partner_name}}: [#happy] That's fair. That's fair. I'll grow on you.
=> END

~ trail_crew
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] One thing, though. Up there, keep an eye on this parcel.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] Not everybody who carries mail carries it honest.
{{partner_name}}: [#angry] There's a bunch that call themselves the Shortcut Crew.
{{partner_name}}: [#angry] They'll take a job right out of your hands and sell it back to you.
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] But hey. What are the odds, right?
=> END

~ rise
# On the rise, the held view of Highbank below. The first line is from before.
The trail climbs. Up ahead, Highbank's roofs catch the first of the sun.
# NEW, proposal (Claude, 2026-10-26): the view from the rise.
The trees open. Down below, Highbank's lamps are going out one by one, and chimney smoke climbs straight up.
And over all of it stands a tower, taller than anything you've ever seen.
{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] ...Every time. Every single time, that thing gets me.
{{partner_name}}: [#happy] That's the Wayline Tower. On a clear day you can see it three bends down the river.
=> END
